# udev rule: give the SHT45 Trinkey's SCPI (data) serial port a stable name.
#
# Result: /dev/sht45 always points at the data CDC port, regardless of plug
# order or how many other serial devices are present.
#
# --- Install -------------------------------------------------------------
#   1. Discover the product id and serial of YOUR Trinkey:
#        udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyACM0 | grep -E 'idVendor|idProduct|serial'
#      (or: lsusb -v -d 239a: | grep -E 'idProduct|iSerial')
#   2. Fill in idProduct and serial below.
#   3. sudo cp 99-sht45-trinkey.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#      sudo udevadm control --reload && sudo udevadm trigger
#   4. Replug the Trinkey; `ls -l /dev/sht45` should appear.
#
# Notes:
#   * idVendor 239a = Adafruit. Fill in idProduct for the SHT4x Trinkey.
#   * ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02" selects the DATA port (SCPI). The console
#     port is interface "00". If boot.py uses console=False/data=True there is
#     only one port -- drop the interface match then.
#   * GROUP/MODE make the port readable without root; adjust to taste.

SUBSYSTEM=="tty", \
  ATTRS{idVendor}=="239a", \
  ATTRS{idProduct}=="XXXX", \
  ATTRS{serial}=="XXXXXXXXXXXX", \
  ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", \
  SYMLINK+="sht45", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
